    ('120L','ARCH','4067','This course employs research and analysis of contemporary cases to expose students to the theory and practice of public relations management. Students will learn how to recognize, understand and deliver on various target audiences needs as well as apply lessons learned to various public relations scenarios and critically evaluate organizational communication tactics and the role of professional ethical standards.Offered in fall and spring.','CONTEMPORARY ARCHITECTURE'),
