    ('202N','ART','5414','Explores the global aspects of retail strategies through examination of the economic, geopolitical, cultural, and other factors governing the basic tenets of todays globalized marketplace. Various international regions are analyzed in terms of their market characteristics and current retail environment. U.S retailers operating globally are also discussed and analyzed in detail. Topics include fair trade, free trade, sustainability, and the expansion of the globalized marketing system through multichanneling retailing.','INTERM PAINTING'),
