    ('209N','ART','12555','This is a required course for psychologyeducation certification students to integrate education psychology theory as part of the pre student teaching experience.  The course reinforces the understanding of key concepts of psychology content by examining this content through peer teaching and field experiencees.   Specific implications and application of learning theories will be discussed using examples drawn from educational situations and educational programs.  Emphasis is on behavioral, social, cognitive, information processing, and constructivist theories.  The theme will focus on reflective practice.  No fieldwork required. Corequisite EDUC ','THE ANIMATED SHORT FILM'),
    ('210N','ART','5426','None','ADVANCED ART I'),
