    ('205L','ARTL','5728','This course is the capping course for all Cybersecurity majors. In this course, students will have the opportunity to put into practice the combination of techniques studied throughout the cybersecurity major.  Students will implement a complete cybersecurity project, using skills from both Computer Science and ITS.  During the course, you will assemble a team for the project, gather project requirements, create and track a project plan, present progress status for the project, implement a working prototype for the project and generate system documentation. At the end of the course you will make a final presentation and deliver the system with the corresponding documentation.','MICHELANGELO'),
