    ('400L','COM','6795','This course examines some of the major works that form the literary tradition of Western culture. At least half of the authors will be drawn from the PreChristian, the Medieval, and the Renaissance periods for example, Homer, Sophocles, Virgil, Chaucer, Dante, Shakespeare, and Cervantes. Additional reading from the postRenaissance period may be selected by the instructor. Fulfills a Foundation Requirement for the English major.','GENDER,CULT,COMM'),
