    ('415N','COM','6810','None','IN STUDY:COM'),
    ('416L','COM','6811','ST SPORTS FEATURE WRITINGSports Feature Writing is a practicum course that offers students reallife experience as sports reporters, deploying the practical skills gained from COM  Sports Reporting. Students will cover Marist athletics  either varsity or club sports  by writing indepth feature stories and columns throughout the semester. Those stories will receive a great deal of feedback and editing from the instructor and subsequently be offered to the Center Field website for publication. This hybrid course will meet in person once a week. Students will sharpen their reporting and writing skills and build a portfolio of published work.  Fulfills an upper level communication electivePrerequisite , junior and senior standing','SPEC TOPICS:COMM'),
    ('417L','COM','6812','None','IN ST:COMMUNICATIONS'),
    ('418L','COM','3795','None','COMM CAMPAIGN MANAGEMENT'),
    ('420L','COM','6813','Examines earths natural systems, adverse impacts of human activities upon these systems, and how society addresses these impacts. Topics may include ecology biodiversity forests and deforestation human population growth and control food production sustainable agriculture climate disruption energy resources environmental justice water and air pollution and environmental sustainability. In addition to the science of these topics, related politics, economics, and ethics are discussed. Content, learning approaches and text vary by instructor. Offered each semester.','ADV PUBLIC PRESENT.'),
    ('421L','COM','6814','None','ADV SCREENWRITING'),
    ('422L','COM','3796','None','CASE STUDIES INTEGRATED COMM'),
    ('423L','COM','8926','In this class we will attempt to figure out where human rights reside  with the individual, with the state, with a regional body or on the international level by looking at the historical development of the idea and theory of human rights. We will look at the development of the midth century Universal Declaration of Human Rights guided by Eleanor Roosevelt and its counter, the Arab Charter on Human Rights. We will examine the concept and theory of human rights and arguments for their protection. We will explore human rights violations, and the intergovernmental and nongovernmental organizations that work to alleviate such.','STRATEGIC ADVERT CAMPAIGN DVLP'),
