    ('466L','COM','4589','Designed for bilingual students with some formal training in Spanish and advanced nonheritage speakers, this course stresses improvement of reading, writing, and oral skills in Spanish for formal use. Written assignments are based on excerpts from various literary works. Attention will be given to various forms of official writing styles e.g., business letter, advertising, journalism, radio and television, translation techniques, and to the research and writing of academic essays. Offered when there is sufficient interest.','JOURNALISM WORKSHOP'),
