    ('303L','ECON','7803','This course introduces one of the basic computational tools of calculus the derivative. Functional models, including linear, quadratic, exponential, and logarithmic models are developed. These ideas and techniques are applied to study situations from business and other disciplines. This course is offered every semester. Appropriate technology will be selected by the instructor.','INTERMED MICROECON'),
    ('304L','ECON','7804','This course examines the influences of technology on society and the ethical dilemmas presented by technological advances. Students study major ethical theories to provide a framework for analyzing the impact of technology on current legal, social, economic, governmental, religious, and scientific activities.','INTERMED MACROECO'),
