    ('328L','BIOL','11416','A study of the basic principles of the immune response. The cellular and humoral systems will be analyzed. Topic areas to be covered will include the biology and chemistry of the immune response, complement fixation, immunodiagnoses, immunoassay, immunopathology, autoimmunity, transplant and cancer immunology. Threehour lecture per week. Typically offered every spring.','CELL BIOLOGY'),
