    ('361L','ENG','8297','A course in biological evolution designed for students not majoring in the sciences. Science as a process and how science differs from religion will be examined. Topics include Darwin, natural selection and other mechanisms that cause change, evolutionary medicine, how life began, and selected examples of animal evolution and adaptation. Threehour lecture per week. Note This course may not be taken for credit by students who have completed BIOL .','ROM-ERLY CHR LIT'),
