    ('620L','COMG','6707','This course combines all the skills learned in the previous graduate classes, particularly the strategic and tactical application of marketing communication skills and concepts. The Capstone course project will incorporate skills and research required to inform successful marketing communication initiatives as well as the development of strategies that involve effective and measurable messages and touchpoint integration. The focus is on thinking about the strategic framework and how to apply this framework to guide strategic decisions. The purpose of the course is to solve real world problems and students will have the opportunity to present their marketing communication strategies to a real client at the end of the course.','COMM CFLCT+NEGT'),
