    ('411L','MDIA','5022','ST WOMEN AND ARTThis course will examine the careers of the most productive and influential women artists working in the Western World from the th century to the mid th century.  We will also look at depictions of women by both male and female artists to see how women were viewed, and whether male and female artists reveal different and genderbased attitudes in their art.  For each section of the course, I will provide a handout listing the works of art we will study and the reading assignments from both the textbook and material on reserve in the library.  Notetaking on the reading is strongly advised as the exams will also cover this material.  Fulfills Elective credit','TOPICS IN INTERACTIVE MEDIA'),
    ('421L','MDIA','5007','ST CONCERT EVENT PLANNINGCourse will take students through the process of planning a semester of music concert productions. This course will ask students to participate in audition evaluations, create event publicity, manage frontofhouse experiences, and assist in show stagingcrew operations.','TOPICS IN TELEVISION'),
