    ('101N','ORG','11875','Examines earths natural systems, adverse impacts of human activities upon these systems, and how society addresses these impacts. Topics may include ecology biodiversity forests and deforestation human population growth and control food production sustainable agriculture climate disruption energy resources environmental justice water and air pollution and environmental sustainability. In addition to the science of these topics, related politics, economics, and ethics are discussed. Content, learning approaches and text vary by instructor. Offered each semester.','MANAG &amp;amp; LEADING IN ORGANIZATIO'),
