    ('680N','MATA','12646','Students explore the historic styles and modes of Western dress and adornment throughout the ages from the ancient Egyptian period to the th century. Costume is viewed within the context of the period relating to major historical developments, technology, production, and economic situation. Also discussed are the arts, specific individuals, events, or societal values that can be seen to influence fashions of the times. Fulfills the CoreLS requirement for Fine Arts.','STUDENT TEACHING PRACTICUM'),
