    ('601N','PHTH','11436','STSPORTS MANAGEMENTThe global sports industry is over  billion with  of that in the U.S. This course provides an overview of management principles as they relate to the business of sports, including marketing, finance, economics, legal and ethical principles as they relate to sport management at the high  school, recreational, collegiate, international and professional fields. This course would be of value to students in the School of Management, sports communication, sports medicine or student athletes.','INTRO TO PHYSICAL THERAPY'),
    ('602N','PHTH','11437','An introduction to the French language in its cultural context. Basic communicative skills, pronunciation, essentials of grammar, vocabulary building for everyday conversation, cultural exposure through focused readings and multimedia materials. Two weekly onehour sessions of audio and video practice through  the Language Center are required. Closed to heritage speakers of French and students from countries where French is commonly spoken. Offered annually.','HUMAN PHYSIOLOGY'),
    ('603N','PHTH','11438','A continuation of the elementary course. The basic language skills are pursued more intensively and thoroughly. A better understanding of Italian culture continues. Closed to heritage speakers of Italian. Offered annually.','CRITICAL INQUIRY I'),
