    ('715N','PHTH','11518','This course focuses on building the various critical thinking skills needed for Fashion industry relatedspecific research and development. In this course, students will learn to identify key impact areas withinthe fashion landscape and create opportunities for innovation and meaningful change. Students willintegrate areas such as research, analysis, experimentation, concept development, and design process tocommunicate a range of ideas that address specific problems. Developing a strong analytical frameworkwill allow students to build an understanding of the organizational methods used in presenting a visuallyrich expression of their ideas to demonstrate communication skillsets required in the fashion industrythrough a variety of professional methods, including visual, oral, and written forms.','CUMULATIVE EXAM'),
