    ('485N','SOCW','13216','ST HISTORY OF MEMESThe significance of memes and meme culture is as important as ever. What started as small pockets of niche internet jokes have become virtual internet currency traded between the hands or, eyes of those who get them. Memes are a language, a collection of the internets largest inside jokes, and their importance as a digital communication tool, now more than ever, cannot be stressed enough. Bud Light Seltzer recently hired a chief meme officer, the word meme shows up in job descriptions for roles from homepage editor to social media editor and beyond, and organizations as large and prevalent as the White House are now leaning on memes as a way to both connect with and speak to younger audiences around the world. To truly understand how to use them most effectively, you need to understand where they start, how they come to be and why exactly the biggest ones rise to the top. Studying their history and development can help students stay ahead and be ready for the next level of any mediacentric field, whether it is collecting the best for a journalistic roundup or creating your own to make your written piece or Public Relations stand out. Fulfills Upper level Comm Elective','PRACT SOC WORK II'),
