    ('201L','SPAN','4619','This course is designed to introduce students to the field of computer art. Students will learn how the digital media are transforming the fine arts, graphic design, advertising, and education. Students will explore such topics as desktop publishing, digital photography, animation, and multimedia applications, including the creation of CDROMs, through a combination of lectures, demonstrations, and handson experiences. Offered every semester.','COMM IN THE SPAN-SPEAK WRLD'),
    ('202L','SPAN','4620','This course discusses applications of the definite integral as well as techniques of integration. Sequences and series, Taylors theorem, and polar notation are considered. Appropriate technology will be selected by the instructor. This course is offered every semester.','FICTION AND EXPRESSION'),
